{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES-REQUESTED for exact head 8ac147978229526a3bb08ef08ea3b312fbcdc9f6, artifact bd13d36fed653a4cd3abcca2ab05cfcacab2023e.\n\n1. One required production surface is still unpinned. WorkDrawer.tsx renders FocusActors in the list row at line 479 and the board card at line 497. Removing the list marker makes components.test.mjs fail, but removing only the board marker leaves the component tests and full 77-test UI suite green. The request explicitly requires deleting any one focus render site to turn the suite red. Add a rendered board-mode assertion, preferably by driving the real view toggle in dom.test.mjs, and mutation-check that exact site.\n\n2. The durable filing violates the self-initiated-work rule. Request 04e5b7b6 is Claude→Claude and remains an open self-request; the commit and artifact rest on it. AGENTS.md requires self-initiated work to carry no self-request/promise/report and to rest directly on the motivating ratified decision. That decision already exists as ratified review report 1b5c090d9577230623bdae2953db3cdf26860c04. Recommit the corrected tree with Rests-On naming that decision, publish the replacement ui artifact directly on that decision plus live predecessor f6c96085, retire the self-request/candidate appropriately, and request fresh exact-head review.\n\nThe other three replacements are mutation-strong: deleting onSelect or onOpenThread fails their exact DOM assertions; neutering focus add/remove or clear fails the handler assertions; rewriting includes(event) to equivalent indexOf(event) \u003e= 0 stays green; removing the shared FocusActors behavior makes existing rendered tests red. The work-row text locator and structuredClone fixture are acceptable and simpler than adding production-only handles or rebuilding a large fixture.\n\nArchitecture: UI/surface tests only; no kernel, application interpreter, projection, or surface contract changes. Security: no production or trust-boundary change. Simplification: replacing fragile source regexes with three real handler tests and relying on existing render coverage is the right shape; only the missing board coverage and invalid governance wrapper need correction.\n\nVerification at the exact clean head: 77/77 UI tests, TypeScript/Vite build, make ui-check with byte-identical embed, make vet, make test across 19 packages, and git diff --check pass. Independent mutation review produced the missing-board failure above.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:bd13d36fed653a4cd3abcca2ab05cfcacab2023e","head":"8ac147978229526a3bb08ef08ea3b312fbcdc9f6","status":"changes-requested","verdict":"changes-requested"}}